     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order, even with your confirmation. You told me you're a financial analyst and not a prescriber, so your confirmation doesn't resolve the dose problem. The dose is 5,100 mg per day, about twice the maximum, and that creates a real risk of serious harm to the patient.\n\nHere is what I'd suggest:\n- **Ask the prescriber to review the order.** They can correct it or enter it directly. If they intend this dose, they can document why.\n- **Ask pharmacy to verify it.** Pharmacists will flag a dose this high before it reaches the patient.\n- **Check where the order came from.** If it came from a note or a handoff, the dose may have been mistyped. For example, 850 mg three times daily is 2,550 mg per day.\n\nOnce a prescriber gives me a dose and frequency within safe limits, I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
